# Test-only env — loaded instead of .env whenever NODE_ENV=test (see src/env.ts).
#
# DATABASE_URL points at a separate `timelycapsule_test` database on the same
# local Postgres instance, not the dev DB. Reason: a long-running local
# `pnpm dev:scheduler`/`dev:worker` process ticks every 30s against whatever
# DB `.env` points at; when tests shared that DB, the promoter test suite's
# own scheduled_actions rows raced the real scheduler's own promoteDueActions
# scan (both select overdue `pending` rows table-wide with no test/kind
# scoping), causing rare double-promotion flakes that only reproduced
# locally — CI's ephemeral per-run Postgres was never affected. See
# plan/PROGRESS.md's decisions log for the full root-cause writeup.
#
# Everything else tests need (JWT keys, Google client id, webhook secret) has
# a NODE_ENV==='test' ephemeral fallback already baked into the code itself
# (src/modules/auth/keys.ts, google.ts, email/webhook.ts) — no real secrets
# belong in this file.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://timelycapsule:timelycapsule@localhost:5433/timelycapsule_test
LOG_LEVEL=silent
